# SDG 17 (Partnerships for the Goals) is defined by governance, finance, technology transfer, capacity building, and systemic international collaboration.
# Elsevier treats SDG 17 not as an empirical topic of investigation, but as an operational mode of conducting research (e.g., North-South co-authorships, open science data sharing, international funding grants). Consequently, bibliometric platforms (including Scopus and SciVal) typically analyze SDG 17 via metadata indicators (cross-border co-authorships, public-private co-publications, multi-funder acknowledgments) rather than keyword matching on titles and abstracts.


